# Target C-II — complete-angle affine reduction cuts generic H6 to 5,692 cells

**Date:** 2026-09-19  
**Status:** exact finite reduction; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** degree-pure support-seven generic `H6`, with reciprocal hull `0,1,...,5`, reciprocal interior vertices `6,7`, and no collinear reciprocal triple  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_support7_h6_complete_angle_affine_census_2026_09_19.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The committed ground-coupled affine endpoint is

\[
6{,}308=4{,}936\ C_7+1{,}372\ (C_3\sqcup C_4)
\]

labelled generic-`H6` cells. That relaxation uses the seven local force pentagons, the ground ray order, the fourteen triangles `0ab` associated with present non-ground relation edges, and present non-ground reciprocal triangles. It does not require all eight reciprocal points to share one complete Euclidean angular arrangement.

This note adds that missing affine compatibility layer. Exact Farkas certificates exclude 616 further cells and leave

\[
\boxed{5{,}692=4{,}464\ C_7+1{,}228\ (C_3\sqcup C_4).}
\]

No sine-law metric identity or nonlinear force-closure inequality is used in this count.

## 1. Complete reciprocal angular variables

Fix one surviving generic `H6` oriented-matroid cell. The chirotope determines the strict circular order of the seven rays from each reciprocal vertex.

At each hull vertex `v=0,...,5`, introduce six normalized consecutive ray gaps

\[
h_{v,1},\ldots,h_{v,6}>0.
\]

The ground cone theorem gives

\[
\sum_{p=1}^6h_{0,p}<\frac23,
\]

while strict convexity gives

\[
\sum_{p=1}^6h_{v,p}<1
\qquad(v=1,\ldots,5).
\]

At each interior reciprocal vertex `v=6,7`, introduce seven positive cyclic gaps with

\[
\sum_{p=1}^7h_{v,p}=2.
\]

The chirotope chooses, for each pair of rays at an interior vertex, which cyclic arc is the ordinary angle. The selected arc is required to lie strictly below `1`, i.e. below \(\pi\).

Every normalized reciprocal angle

\[
A_{v;ab}=\frac1\pi\angle avb
\]

is therefore an exact integer-affine expression in these ray gaps.

## 2. Tie the complete angular arrangement to the physical pentagons

For each non-ground reciprocal vertex `v=1,...,7`, keep the five physical force gaps

\[
x_{v,0},\ldots,x_{v,4}.
\]

The already certified pentagon simplex gives

\[
\sum_{k=0}^4x_{v,k}=2,
\qquad
x_{v,k}+x_{v,k+1}-x_{v,k+3}>\frac13.
\]

Exactly five reciprocal rays at `v` correspond to present support edges. Their complete edge signs and the reciprocal chirotope determine the signed-force cyclic order. For every pair among those five rays, the existing audited raw-angle conversion gives the reciprocal angle as an exact integer-affine expression in the five `x` variables. Equating that expression with the corresponding `A_{v;ab}` supplies ten angle ties at each non-ground vertex, hence seventy ties total.

The complete eight-point reciprocal must also satisfy the Euclidean triangle identity for every triple:

\[
\boxed{
A_{a;bc}+A_{b;ac}+A_{c;ab}=1
}
\qquad
\{a,b,c\}\subset\{0,\ldots,7\}.
\]

There are exactly

\[
\binom83=56
\]

such equations. This includes triangles containing missing relation pairs. Those angles exist geometrically even when the pair is not a support edge; omitting them was a relaxation, not a geometric freedom.

The resulting affine system has 85 variables:

- 35 physical force-turn variables;
- 36 hull-ray gap variables;
- 14 interior-ray gap variables.

Its equality family contains seven force-turn sums, two interior full-circle sums, seventy present-ray angle ties, and all fifty-six reciprocal triangle sums. Its strict facets are the thirty-five pentagon-simplex facets, all fifty ray-gap positivity facets, six hull-span facets, and the forty-two ordinary-angle `<pi` facets at the two interior reciprocal vertices.

## 3. Exact exclusion certificate

Write the equality system as

\[
E_r(z)=b_r
\]

and every strict facet as

\[
f_j(z)=c_j+a_j\cdot z>0.
\]

The verifier asks HiGHS only for a candidate dual. A cell is excluded only if the candidate can be converted to exact rational coefficients satisfying

\[
\alpha_j\ge0,
\qquad
\sum_j\alpha_j=1,
\]

and

\[
\sum_j\alpha_j a_j+
\sum_r\mu_rE_r=0
\]

coefficientwise in all 85 variables. On the equality space this forces

\[
\sum_j\alpha_jf_j(z)=\kappa.
\]

The verifier accepts the exclusion only when the exact rational value obeys

\[
\kappa\le0.
\]

Since the left side is a convex combination of strictly positive facets, such a cell is impossible.

All 616 accepted certificates in this reduction have

\[
\boxed{\kappa=0.}
\]

There are no failed exactifications among the proposed exclusions. The largest denominator occurring in an accepted exact dual coefficient is 102.

