## 5. What remains

The 616 eliminated cells fail before metric-length consistency is imposed: they cannot support one complete generic reciprocal angle arrangement compatible with all seven local physical pentagon simplex constraints.

The 5,692 survivors are only survivors of this affine relaxation. They are not certified reciprocal configurations. The complete-metric note supplies fifteen independent sine-law consistency equations on the non-ground `K_7`, and the physical pentagon work supplies the ten exact gap-order cones together with rank-conditioned rational secant cuts for the sharp nonlinear two-gap closure bound. Those are the next two non-affine layers to intersect with this 5,692-cell endpoint.

Reciprocal-collinearity walls remain outside the generic calculation and still require their own branch. No theorem-state file is changed here; C-II remains open.
